R-PB10 R-CM8 R-FL12 R-EC2 R-DI5 R-FL6 (slice 218b): the exit 2 stops of `tln probe --smoke`, one fault in each run (the order of Q586: the first fault gives the message; a line with 2 faults is not tested). Runs 1 to 5, 9 and 10 stop in `ProbeSmoke.read`: no call after the prelude of a failure (`args`, `env_all`, `tty`): no operand, `--range`, `--share`, a bundle file (the operand ends with `.tar.zst` and is not a URL), 2 operands, and (run 9) a URL with no version (R-DI5: `Ident.of_url` refuses it) and (run 10) a URL with `--file` (Q591, R-FL6: a URL uses no project). Run 11: a platform whose header has no `targets` section: after the header read, exit 2 `no target to build` (Q587).
Run 6: `--target` with no `--smoke` (R-FL12: `--target` works with `--smoke` only), the same stop. Run 7: a target that the platform header has not (`riscv`; the first target of the line is a good one): the stop is after the header read, so no build and no `random` for a temp dir; the text lists the targets of the header. Run 8: the URL of a package: after the header read, `BuildTarget.targets_of` has no section: not a platform, exit 2, no build.
